891
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:18,050
Something Precious

892
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:28,000
This bank, as well?

893
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,100
I heard those guys have been going around the branch offices, 
redeeming their money for gold all day.

894
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,100
What?!

895
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,800
"Due to unforeseen circumstances, 
this branch is temporarily closed"?!

896
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,880
How can you do that to us?!

897
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,290
So, the rumors really were true...

898
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:45,560
These banknotes are just 
worthless scraps of paper now!

899
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,800
You still haven't found out 
where the bills are coming from?

900
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:54,310
No, we haven't pinpointed 
the factory that's printing them.

901
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:56,610
But we have figured out who's behind it!

902
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,570
It's Yukime, sir!

903
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:01,830
The she-fox that rules 
the White Tower in Lawless City!

904
00:03:01,830 --> 00:03:07,380
A carriage from the Snow Fox Corporation was used 
to transport the gold coins that had been exchanged.

905
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:10,800
And the Snow Fox Corporation happens to be 
the public face of the White Tower.

906
00:03:11,170 --> 00:03:12,420
<i>It's a coincidence.</i>

907
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:14,420
And the route that they used 
to transport the money

908
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:16,760
<i>No... I knew that she had 
stooped to prostitution.</i><i></i>

909
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:16,760
is an exact match for the counterfeit bill routes 
we've been investigating.

910
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:23,770
Is... Is something the matter, sir?

911
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:41,920
Stop...

912
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:42,700
Sir?

913
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:45,900
Stop... the carriage.

914
00:03:56,720 --> 00:04:01,010
He has ascended to heights 
that only he can attain.

915
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:04,500
He doesn't need me anymore.

916
00:04:06,910 --> 00:04:09,690
The fall of the Major Corporate Alliance 
is inevitable.

917
00:04:10,210 --> 00:04:14,900
They've forced closure of all their storefronts, 
bringing the citizens' unrest to its peak.

918
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:17,650
Riots are breaking out 
at each of their bank branches.

919
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,340
Customers are bearing down on ours, as well.

920
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:23,920
They're demanding to exchange their money, 
and we're struggling to control the situation.

921
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,160
Can we weather the storm?

922
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:27,310
If things carry on like this,

923
00:04:27,310 --> 00:04:30,710
it will only be a few days 
before our bank vault is empty.

924
00:04:30,710 --> 00:04:34,400
Even with all our domestic 
and foreign assets combined,

925
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,010
we won't survive a credit collapse.

926
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,840
I see.

927
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:41,600
But it's all right!

928
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:44,960
If we provide something to give 
the marketplace a sense of security,

929
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:47,710
surely we can put a stop 
to this catastrophe!

930
00:04:47,710 --> 00:04:49,250
For example... I know!

931
00:04:49,250 --> 00:04:51,630
We could show them 
we have giant stacks of gold coins...

932
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:52,810
Forget it.

933
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:55,800
It doesn't matter anymore.

934
00:04:57,010 --> 00:04:59,950
<i>He</i> is the one who put 
the counterfeit bills in circulation.

935
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:02,800
The one who caused the credit collapse.

936
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:05,740
This is what he wanted.

937
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:08,210
He has forsaken us.

938
00:05:08,210 --> 00:05:11,200
